 fat burn  throughout the day we should be looking  at improving the biggest contributor to  our tdee which is our bmr here are the  top 3 workout modes to improve your bmr  strength training is a mode of training  that helps you increase your muscular  strength and build lean muscle mass  strength training is important because  your bmr is largely determined by your  total lean muscle mass so muscle mass  burns more calories than fat for every  pound of lean muscle mass your body  burns an additional 14 calories a day  whereas a pound of fat only burns 2 to 3  calories hence the more lean muscle you  have on your body the higher your bmr  will be which increases your body's fat  burning ability  examples of strength training includes  exercises with gym machines or free  weights such as dumbbells barbells  kettlebells or equipment such as a  resistance band or even body weight  exercises such as push-ups and pull-ups  so those who add strength training two  to three times a week burns  significantly more fat than those who  only perform cardio exercises  high intensity interval training or more  commonly known as hit involves quick  intense burst of activity some common  exercises used in a heat session are  burpees squat jumps and sprinting  the whole goal is to push your body into  an anaerobic state and for you to empty  your tank this will not only help you  burn tons of calories in a short period  of time however  it will also help keep your metabolism  elevated even after your workout is over  through a process called excess post  exercise oxygen consumption  epoc or more commonly known as the after  burn effect  this refers to all of the oxygen and  energy in the form of calories that your  body takes in and uses after exercise to  help repair your muscles and recover the  afterburn effect can last up to 36 hours  therefore heat has become a famous  training mode as it is known to help  fire up your metabolism throughout the  entire day  [Music]  compound exercises are multi-joint  movements that are designed to target  multiple muscle groups at one time  examples of compound movements include  squat to shoulder press lunges push-ups  and plank roll  most compound exercises will not only  challenge your muscular fitness but it  will also get your heart rate up and  improve your cardio fitness while  burning lots of calories to simplify how  doing compound exercises could boost  your metabolism let us look at our  muscles as a factory the more muscles we  work at one time the more energy is  needed to power the factory thus  increasing our body's metabolism so most  of my workout videos are based on  compound movements do check them out on  my youtube channel and they are perfect  especially for those of you who have  very limited time right now that you  know the right type of workouts to start  including into your fitness routine let  us not neglect the most important aspect  to weight loss which is our food here  are my top 5 functional foods that are  known to help you boost your metabolism  [Music]  as mentioned previously our metabolism  is linked to our muscle mass therefore  it is important to always fill our  muscles with the protein it needs the  guideline to follow is that 20 to 30  percent of your total daily calories  should come from protein  this can be easily met by including a  serving of protein such as lean meat  fish  nuts legumes or yogurt at every meal and  snack this in turn will ensure that our  muscles continue to efficiently function  as a powerhouse to burn fat as fuel  throughout the day  on top of that did you know that protein  causes the largest rice in thermic  effect of feeding  in comparison to carbs or fats  this is because protein takes longer for  the body to break down which means that  it needs more calories to digest absorb  and process the nutrients in your meals  it can increase your metabolic rate by  fifteen to thirty percent compared to  five to ten percent for cups and only  zero to three percent for fats  therefore consuming plenty of protein  can make you burn an extra 150 to 200  calories in a day plus you will feel  full and prevent overeating  studies have shown that caffeine in  coffee can boost metabolism by three to  eleven percent  this is why if you were to take a look  at fat burners most of them have  caffeine as the number one ingredient  now that doesn't mean that you should  just be sipping on coffee all day long  and be a caffeine addict and expect to  lose weight you still need to put the  effort in drinking a cup of black coffee  before a workout can improve your  workout performance speed up your  metabolism hence help you burn fat more  efficiently and that's something i  personally practice one cup of coffee  right before my training session  this next food is probably one of your  favorite desserts dark chocolate yup  dark chocolate is definitely one of the  yummiest snacks out there that can help  you boost your metabolism the  monounsaturated fats present in dark  chocolate is not only known to boost  your metabolism but also improve your  gut flora thus improving digestion in  addition dark chocolate also contains an  amino acid called tryptophan that your  brain uses to produce the  neurotransmitter serotonin which can  increase feelings of overall happiness  now burn fat and feeling happy at the  same time this is my go-to snack so the  next time you crave for dessert opt for  a small amount of dark chocolate  capsaicin found in chili peppers are  known to help boost metabolism by  slightly increasing the rate at which  your body burns calories  studies have shown that they may help  your body burn around 50 extra calories  per day besides that according to a  review of studies in nearly 200 people  consuming at least 2 milligrams of  capsaicin directly before each meal  appears to reduce calorie consumption  especially from carbs so  spice up your meals and turn up the fat  burn mode  we all know the importance of water but  did you know that your body needs water  to process calories hence if you're even  slightly dehydrated your metabolism may  slow down experts suggest that drinking  8 to 10 glasses of water per day would  increase your daily energy demand by at  least 95 calories so  keep yourself hydrated throughout the  day some really simple tricks to drink  more water daily is to drink a glass  once you're up in the morning and drink  a glass of water before every meal or  consume a healthy vegetable soup before  your meal and also snack on fresh fruits  and vegetables which naturally contain  water  water helps to fill you up which means  those who drank more water will tend to  eat less food  now what you want to avoid are sugary  drinks and alcohol as they contain empty  calories but can add up over time and  cause weight gain although almost all  foods will increase your metabolism  these are some top foods that can give  you a good kick to your metabolic rate  and help you burn more calories provided  that you add sufficient amount of  physical activity with it even though we  often link metabolism with weight loss  metabolism is responsible for so much  more such as having energy mental  clarity and it is essentially the  foundation of everything we do hence  remember that a healthy metabolism is  the first step in helping your body in  burning fat more efficiently throughout  the day and this is fundamentally  achieved by pairing an active lifestyle  with a well-balanced diet so i hope you  enjoyed this video i hope that you have  learned some tips and tricks to start  implementing into your fitness routine  and if you like this video do give this  video a thumbs up and don't forget to  hit the subscribe button if you haven't  yet done it go on to my youtube channel  and check out a lot more workout videos  and nutrition tips fitness tips as well  as healthy recipes and i will see you in  my next video  all the best

